</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><h2 style="text-align:left"><b><strong>Step 2: Reading the dataset</strong></b></h2><p dir="ltr"><span>In this step we load the dataset and encode disease labels into numbers and visualize class distribution to check for imbalance. We then use </span><a href="https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/imbalanced-learn-module-in-python/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code><span>RandomOverSampler</span></code><span> </span></a><span>to balance the dataset by duplicating minority classes and ensuring all diseases have equal samples for fair and effective model training.</span></p>
<p dir="ltr"><b><strong>You can download dataset from here : </strong></b><a href="https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20250415160347722782/improved_disease_dataset.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><b><strong>Click here</strong></b></a><b><strong>.</strong></b></p>
